    Fix actionable-card Submit 403 when Entra token omits the user email
    
    Microsoft's v1.0 Actions token does not always carry the acting user's email
    (preferred_username/upn/unique_name all absent), so submitter_email resolved to
    "unknown" and the Step-3 "submitter must match the card email" check always
    403'd on Submit (Refresh was unaffected — it falls back to the body email).
    
    Only enforce the strict identity match when the token actually provides an
    email; otherwise rely on the cryptographically verified Microsoft caller (azp)
    plus the Step-3a team-membership check. Also dump the token identity claims on
    successful verification to reveal which claim (if any) carries the user.
    
