[33mcommit 3b639e0a36154d5a867eca8f730029361049da62[m
Author: Manish Soni <Manish.Soni@dynatechconsultancy.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 9 14:39:31 2026 +0530

    Accept v1.0 issuer + unique_name for actionable-card Entra tokens
    
    Microsoft's Actions service sends a v1.0 token (iss https://sts.windows.net/
    <tenant>/) rather than v2.0, so issuer validation rejected it with 401
    "Invalid issuer" even though signature, audience and azp all matched. Validate
    the issuer manually against BOTH the v1.0 (sts.windows.net) and v2.0
    (login.microsoftonline.com/.../v2.0) forms (PyJWT's issuer= accepts one value).
    
    Also read the acting user's email from unique_name (v1.0 claim) in addition to
    preferred_username/upn/email across all three handlers, so submit attribution
    still works with v1.0 tokens.
    
